@format 1
@id merge.create-group-drop
@title Create merge group from empty-area drop
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Drop source files or a dragged group item onto the empty group-panel area to create a new merge group.
@section I. UI
@tabs Merge
@flow TB
@related merge.move-file, merge.auto-group

@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup

[input] Empty group-panel area receives a drop <input>
- Receive external files, list paths, or a dragged group item @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
> collect

[collect] Collect paths for the new group <decision>
- For a dragged group item, remove its matching source path from the original group @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
- For external files, request supported media paths before grouping @ group.PGroupPathsRead(...)
? "No usable path is collected" > unchanged
? "One or more paths are collected" > create

[create] Add a new group <process>
- Create a default-named group and insert each collected path @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
- Rebuild group cards; an emptied source group remains in the model @ group.PGroupRebuild(...)
> result

[result] New merge group visible <output>
= The collected paths form a new group at the end of the merge-group list.

[unchanged] Groups unchanged <output>
= The empty-area drop did not yield a usable path.
